7-92.", "The window glass mesh uses pale blue window glass, an opaque default Principled material; the saved-state extraction reports an unlinked base-color input, and the script sets color and roughness. The hex pattern is actual curves with fine grey hexagonal joints rather than a mapped image texture. No texture coordinate or directional mapping is used by the authored material function. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1430-1435; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/detailed_state.json:469174-469220; /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-8,18-21,27-45.", "The extracted state has only unpacked Blender viewer images with empty paths and no missing external images; no evidence of a full-reference image plane. A Principled BSDF-to-Material Output link is present in extracted material state. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/detailed_state.json:470250-470290; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:5-7; /evidence/final_source/build.py:1-92."],\n52\t  "geometry_analysis": ["The chair backs are custom curved meshes with Solidify and Subdivision modifiers, and their seats, five radial rods and caster spheres are separate meshes. Tables have thin tops and legs; lamp shades are cones on stems and feet. These constructions are editable, but the existence of parts does not prove contact or connectivity. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:46-82.", "Independent extraction lists 221 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections or support errors; no student surface-contact verification is recorded. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-11; /evidence/sdk_events.json:1-138."],\n53\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n54\t    {"gt_instance_ids": [63], "gt_semantic_label": "floor", "student_object_names": ["floor"], "confidence": 