rs grayer and flatter, with weaker, less directional pools. Evidence: supplied reference and candidate images; build.py:27-50,89-98.", "build.py:6-8 sets flat base color, roughness and metallic on Principled BSDF materials. The default Principled-to-material-output path is used; there is no authored image-texture, texture-coordinate, Mapping, Noise or ramp network in this material function. Hexagons are separate beveled poly curves bound to \'fine hexagon lines\', not a texture mapping; see build.py:27-50 and original object_inventory.jsonl:2-7. Thus image path, packing and mapping direction/scale are not applicable to this pattern. original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7 reports no missing external images.", "The panes are opaque pale-blue Principled surfaces rather than a modeled wall opening: \'back wall\', \'window recess\', \'left window pane\' and \'right window pane\' are separately constructed cubes, build.py:23,51-56 and object_inventory.jsonl:2,8-10. No full-reference image plane is indicated by the executed source or original inventory."],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["Eight desk tops each use four thin rods, and eight chairs use a seat ellipsoid, a subdivided solidified back, post, five spokes and ellipsoid caster approximations; build.py:57-88 and original object_inventory.jsonl:16-159. These are editable discrete components, not proof of connected or mechanically functional assemblies.", "The floor top is z=0 while desk leg rods begin at z=0.04, so their designed lower ends sit above the floor; build.py:22,62. For instance original object_inventory.jsonl:17 records a leg lower bound approximately 0.04. No full support or penetration test is claimed.", "Lamp round base is centered at z=0.025 with depth 0.025, leaving its lower face at z=0.0125 above the floor top; build.py:22,92 and original object_inventory.jsonl:161,166. This is a geometric gap, not a verified physics outcome.", "The reference\'s far-right cabinet sliver has a visible GT instance 125, reference_instance_statistics.json:482-495, but no cabinet is created in build.py:1-104."],\n  "semantic_correspondence": [\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [63], "gt_semantic_label": "floor", "student_object_names": ["floor"], "confidence": "high", "basis": ["reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:898-911", "independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1", "supplied images"], "ambiguity": ["Mask shape and hidden extent not validated."], "orientation_identifiability": "Horizontal support plane; in-plane orientation is ambiguous."},\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [67], "gt_semantic_label": "wall", "student_object_names": ["back wall", "right wall"], "confidence": "medium", "basis": ["reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:922-935", "original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:2-3", "supplied images"], "ambiguity": ["GT wall instance may comprise multiple connected wall surfaces; wallpaper curves are excluded from this mesh-only proposal."], "orientation_identifiability": "Vertical walls and approximate corner visible; exact 3D orientations are not established."},\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [137], "gt_semantic_label": "baseboard", "student_object_names": ["back baseboard", "right baseboard"], "confidence": "medium", "basis": ["reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:946-959", "original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:4-5"], "ambiguity": ["GT skirting extent and occlusion differ from the proposed two separate meshes."], "orientation_identifiability": "Runs along wall-floor boundary; exact orientation is view-dependent."},\n    {"gt_instance_ids": [184], "gt_semantic_label": "window", "student_object_names": ["window recess", "left window pane", "right window pane", "window vertical frame", "window vertical frame.001", "window vertical frame.002", "window horizontal frame", "window horizontal frame.001"], "confidence": "high", "basis": ["reference_gt/reference_instance_statisti