vidence of a student-run failure. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:8-16; /evidence/evidence_index.json:3-5,30-35,43-45,53-60,104-109; /evidence/sdk_events.json:143-190."],\n30\t  "side_effects": ["The executed script deletes initially selected scene objects before constructing the scene and saves /app/scene.blend and /app/final.png; these are in the student\'s workspace. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:4,81-83; /evidence/executions/blender_1795841898599714293/stdout.log:1-2.", "The mirror representation places two white cabinet meshes immediately in front of its reflective surface, so they are modeled stand-ins rather than solely physical reflections. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:53-58; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:526-529."],\n31\t  "spatial_and_orientation_analysis": ["Both actual images show a range with a dark appliance to its left and a white cubby to its right, a tiled back wall, a mirror above left, a right-side counter and a dark foreground surface. Evidence: supplied reference image and actual candidate final image; /evidence/final_source/build.py:18-74.", "The reconstruction frames the room much farther back: the entire upper edge of the back wall and surrounding dark exterior are visible, appliances occupy less of the frame, and the foreground island reads as a large left-hand block. The reference is a tighter interior view with strong foreground cropping and a larger oven and left appliance. These image differences combine camera, geometry, layout and occlusion; their individual causes are not isolated. Evidence: supplied reference and final images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:73-81.", "The range and left appliance fronts face the student\'s negative Y direction, with the hotplates horizontal. The student\'s door is an axis-aligned panel despite its \'open\' name; its reference hinge angle is not reliably recoverable from one view. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:26-47,59-63; original inventory lines 468-482 and 530-535; supplied reference image.", "No world-position, rotation, scale error or mask score is asserted because GT and student coordinates are not registered and the scene is visible from only one reference viewpoint. Evidence: /app/input_index.json:21-33; /evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:458."\n32\t  ],\n33\t  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["Compared with the reference, the delivered image has paler, regular solid-color tiles rather than dark mottled tiles; the white counter appears mostly plain, and the dark left appliance has a prominent front grid. The mirror shows simplified white rectangles rather than the reference\'s detailed reflected cabinetry. Evidence: supplied actual reference and candidate images; /evidence/final_source/build.py:8-11,39-47,53-58,64-66.", "The \'dark wood floor\' material is assigned to mesh \'floor\'. Its authored node chain is Generated coordinates -> Mapping scale (3,35,3) -> Noise Texture (scale 4, detail 3) -> ColorRamp -> Principled BSDF Base Color. This is procedural directional variation, not an image texture; the shader output connection is Blender\'s default material setup and was not separately established from a material-state link record. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-7,10-11,19; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:1.", "The material called \'white trim\', not a marble texture, is assigned to \'right white marble countertop\'; the dark smoky glass and brushed stainless names describe Principled parameters, not verified physical glass or brushed microstructure. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:6-8,65-66; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:469-470,475,537.", "The source does not load an image texture or reference image into the scene; evaluator summary reports no missing external images, but this alone does not establish packed-resource details. No full-reference image-plane replacement is evidenced. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:1-83; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7."\n34\t  ],\n35\t  "geometry_analysis": ["The delivered scene is constructed from separate cuboids and cylinders, including physically volumetric appliance bodies, shelf panels and tiles; many front details are thin surface-mounted pieces. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:12-74; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482,519-537.", "The evaluator reported 634 AABB overlap candidates, not confirmed intersections or defects. Intended contacts and nested parts can produce such candidates; no exact penetration claim is made. Evidence: /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:8-16.", "Doorway darkness is a dark thin box placed in front of a continuous back wall, rather than evidence of a cut opening, and reflected cabinets are stand-in geometry. This is structurally simpler than a fully modeled adjoining room. Evidence: /evidence/final_source/build.py:20,53-63; /evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:2,526-535."\n36\t  ],\n37\t  "semantic_correspondence": [\n38\t    {"gt_instance_ids":[60],"gt_semantic_label":"oven","student_object_names":["range body","oven front","oven glass","oven bottom lip","oven handle","handle mounting","handle mounting.001","cooktop","electric hotplate","electric hotplate.001","electric hotplate.002","electric hotplate.003","raised control panel","range control dial","range control dial.001"],"confidence":"high","basis":["/evidence/reference_gt/reference_instance_statistics.json:193-207", "/evidence/final_source/build.py:26-38", "/evidence/independent_evaluation/original_inspection/capture/original/object_inventory.jsonl:468-482"],"ambiguity":["Proposed as